WEBVTT

00:00:12.097 --> 00:00:13.890
Well, that went sideways.

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:16.559
[Tarantula] Susan, you were amazing.

00:00:16.643 --> 00:00:18.103
[Piranha] Where'd you learn
to drive like that?

00:00:18.186 --> 00:00:19.979
I used to deliver pizzas.

00:00:20.063 --> 00:00:23.149
Got canned for being too fast. [chuckles]

00:00:23.233 --> 00:00:25.151
Cool.

00:00:25.235 --> 00:00:26.402
[sniffs, clears throat]

00:00:26.486 --> 00:00:27.529
-Your breath stinks.
-What?

00:00:27.612 --> 00:00:29.531
What do you brush
your teeth with, sardines?

00:00:29.614 --> 00:00:31.491
-[laughing]
-That's a burn.

00:00:31.574 --> 00:00:32.992
I don't brush my teeth with anything.

00:00:33.076 --> 00:00:34.577
-Shocking.
-[laughing]

00:00:35.161 --> 00:00:36.412
[Piranha] That's kind of bad.

00:00:36.496 --> 00:00:37.956
I'm surprised you hang out with me.

00:00:38.039 --> 00:00:39.165
-How about a mint?
-Ooh!

00:00:39.249 --> 00:00:40.792
-[Piranha] That's clutch.
-Yes, please.

00:00:40.875 --> 00:00:41.876
I'll take two.

00:00:42.669 --> 00:00:44.629
Uh, what about you, Wolf? Mint?

00:00:45.171 --> 00:00:46.506
I'm good. Thanks.

00:00:46.589 --> 00:00:48.049
So, how'd you guys meet anyway?

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:50.844
Spill it. Spill it.

00:00:50.927 --> 00:00:52.971
-Okay, well, uh--
-Well...

00:00:53.054 --> 00:00:54.681
-You tell it.
-No, no, you tell it better.

00:00:54.764 --> 00:00:56.057
Yeah, but you do all the voices.

00:00:56.141 --> 00:00:57.392
And, like, you're so good at it.

00:00:57.475 --> 00:00:58.518
Can somebody tell it?

00:00:58.601 --> 00:01:00.145
Okay, okay.

00:01:00.228 --> 00:01:01.896
It's a funny story.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:04.649
["Crimson and Clover" playing]

00:01:06.484 --> 00:01:09.070
-Hey, kid, are you gonna eat that?
-You gonna eat that?

00:01:09.154 --> 00:01:10.155
What?

00:01:12.866 --> 00:01:13.992
Hey.

00:01:14.075 --> 00:01:15.618
Um... [chuckles]

00:01:15.702 --> 00:01:16.703
Mix-up.

00:01:20.915 --> 00:01:23.001
-[music ends]
-[Shark, Tarantula gag]

00:01:23.084 --> 00:01:24.878
Why is she in his mouth?

00:01:24.961 --> 00:01:26.588
Anyway, that's how we met.

00:01:26.671 --> 00:01:28.965
But that's nothing compared to
our first date when we were--

00:01:29.048 --> 00:01:31.801
No. Stop. Stop, stop, stop, stop, stop.

00:01:31.885 --> 00:01:33.469
All right, all right, all right. Got it.

00:01:33.553 --> 00:01:35.763
Love triumphs over all, and that's great.

00:01:35.847 --> 00:01:37.765
But right now,
we need to focus on the fact

00:01:37.849 --> 00:01:40.894
that every cop in the state
thinks we're the Phantom Bandit.

00:01:40.977 --> 00:01:43.730
Hmm. Not much of a romantic, are you?

00:01:43.813 --> 00:01:45.523
Don't mind him, Sugar Beak.

00:01:45.607 --> 00:01:46.649
He's a little touchy.

00:01:46.733 --> 00:01:49.485
Uh, he's been friend-zoned
by the governor.

00:01:49.569 --> 00:01:51.696
I have not been friend-zoned by the...

00:01:52.739 --> 00:01:53.740
I need a phone.

00:01:55.909 --> 00:01:57.619
[reporter] Madam Governor. Madam Governor.

00:01:57.702 --> 00:02:00.205
How soon are the Bad Guys
going back to prison?

00:02:00.288 --> 00:02:04.000
Please, let's not jump to conclusions
before we have all the facts.

00:02:04.083 --> 00:02:06.753
Thank you, that's all
the questions for now.

00:02:06.836 --> 00:02:09.297
All right, Diane. It's time to
implement damage control.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:11.424
I'm gonna tell the press
there's no more questions--

00:02:11.507 --> 00:02:12.634
Hang on, Maureen.

00:02:12.717 --> 00:02:17.138
Aunt Linda! What a pleasant surprise.

00:02:17.222 --> 00:02:18.890
Wolf, what were you thinking?

00:02:18.973 --> 00:02:20.725
[Wolf on phone] Diane, listen. Uh...

00:02:20.808 --> 00:02:22.143
<i>We hit a little bit of trouble.</i>

00:02:22.227 --> 00:02:23.645
Oh, which part?

00:02:23.728 --> 00:02:25.521
Assaulting the police commissioner

00:02:25.605 --> 00:02:28.983
or stealing a priceless belt
in front of thousands of people?

00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:30.193
It's not what it looks like.

00:02:30.276 --> 00:02:32.612
Someone's setting us up.
You gotta believe me.

00:02:32.695 --> 00:02:34.405
[Diane on phone] Of course I believe you.

00:02:34.489 --> 00:02:37.075
[sighs] Well, you might be the only one.

00:02:37.158 --> 00:02:39.369
Listen, we could really
use your help right now.

00:02:39.452 --> 00:02:41.704
Wolf, I can't call off the cops.

00:02:41.788 --> 00:02:42.997
There's too much heat on you.

00:02:43.081 --> 00:02:44.207
[on phone] / know. I know. I know.

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:46.209
If you could just give me
something to work with,

00:02:46.292 --> 00:02:48.461
a clue, a starting place, something.

00:02:48.544 --> 00:02:49.712
<i>Ion phone) All I know is,</i>

00:02:49.796 --> 00:02:52.215
<i>it's got something to do with
that MacGuffinite thing.</i>

00:02:52.298 --> 00:02:54.550
MacGuffinite? Really?

00:02:54.634 --> 00:02:57.220
Yeah. It's what the Bandit's
been after the whole time.

00:02:57.303 --> 00:02:59.722
I hate to drag you into this,
but it's our only lead.

00:02:59.806 --> 00:03:01.766
-Can you look into it?
-[sirens blaring]

00:03:03.351 --> 00:03:05.520
Yeah, I know exactly who to ask.

00:03:05.603 --> 00:03:07.397
-[on phone] You do?
-Listen to me.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:09.857
I need you to lay low until
I get to the bottom of this.

00:03:09.941 --> 00:03:13.403
In the meantime, don't trust anyone.

00:03:13.945 --> 00:03:16.322
-And, Wolf...
-[on phone] Yeah?

00:03:16.406 --> 00:03:18.533
We'll get through this, okay?

00:03:19.325 --> 00:03:21.244
[sighs] I hope so.

00:03:21.327 --> 00:03:23.496
Hey. I owe you one.

00:03:25.415 --> 00:03:27.125
What are medium friends for, huh?

00:03:27.834 --> 00:03:29.043
[chuckles]

00:03:29.127 --> 00:03:30.128
Yeah.

00:03:32.297 --> 00:03:34.132
[breathes deeply]

00:03:34.966 --> 00:03:36.718
-Maureen?
-Yes, ma'am?

00:03:36.801 --> 00:03:38.886
-Cancel my appointments.
-You got it, ma'am.

00:03:41.139 --> 00:03:42.932
[jazzy music plays]

00:03:44.058 --> 00:03:46.936
I've gotta catch up with an old friend.

00:03:57.030 --> 00:03:58.072
[Wolf] Good news, gang.

00:03:58.156 --> 00:03:59.824
Diane's gonna help us clear our names.

00:04:00.325 --> 00:04:01.826
All we gotta do is lay low and--

00:04:02.744 --> 00:04:04.537
[mysterious music plays]

00:04:06.581 --> 00:04:07.957
-[snores]
-[chair creaks]

00:04:08.624 --> 00:04:10.043
You.

00:04:10.126 --> 00:04:13.421
You should've taken the mint, Whiskers.

00:04:13.504 --> 00:04:14.547
Hey!

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:16.341
Hey...

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:20.303
Hiya, boss. Yeah, the chickens
are in the broiler.

00:04:20.386 --> 00:04:24.057
Repeat, the chickens
are in the broiler. [echoes]

00:04:30.271 --> 00:04:31.606
[Wolf groans]

00:04:33.858 --> 00:04:35.151
I had a...

00:04:36.235 --> 00:04:38.654
What? Where... Where are we?

00:04:38.738 --> 00:04:40.782
What's happening?

00:04:42.784 --> 00:04:43.785
[chains grinding]

00:04:46.662 --> 00:04:52.668
Once upon a time,
there was a big, bad wolf.

00:04:54.295 --> 00:04:56.130
Love that guy.

00:04:56.214 --> 00:04:58.591
What a character.

00:04:58.674 --> 00:05:01.552
He's the one who challenges
the status quo,

00:05:01.636 --> 00:05:03.513
who takes the big chance.

00:05:04.097 --> 00:05:05.848
Without him, shoot,

00:05:05.932 --> 00:05:07.975
I don't even think we have a story.

00:05:08.601 --> 00:05:11.979
And they call him the villain. Hmm.

00:05:12.063 --> 00:05:13.940
Kind of backwards, don't you think?

00:05:14.774 --> 00:05:15.900
Do I know you?

00:05:16.484 --> 00:05:18.653
They call me the Phantom Bandit.

00:05:18.736 --> 00:05:20.613
Nice ring to it, I guess.

00:05:20.696 --> 00:05:24.325
But you can call me Kitty Kat.

00:05:24.409 --> 00:05:26.160
I think you met my girls.

00:05:26.244 --> 00:05:27.954
-Hello!
-Holy shrimp.

00:05:28.037 --> 00:05:29.205
I'm Pigtail.

00:05:29.288 --> 00:05:31.958
It was great honor
to kick the butts of my heroes!

00:05:32.041 --> 00:05:34.752
The butts were even greater
than my dreams. [giggles]

00:05:34.836 --> 00:05:36.712
[chuckles] She's a huge fan.

00:05:36.796 --> 00:05:38.005
Big crime nerd.

00:05:38.798 --> 00:05:40.842
Thanks. I think.

00:05:40.925 --> 00:05:42.343
[blades cutting]

00:05:43.469 --> 00:05:44.720
Oh, hey, Susan!

00:05:44.804 --> 00:05:46.013
Actually...

00:05:46.097 --> 00:05:47.348
Hey!

00:05:49.183 --> 00:05:51.018
-It's Doom.
-Uh...

00:05:51.102 --> 00:05:52.603
Susan is an alias.

00:05:54.397 --> 00:05:56.858
-You lied to me.
-That's all right, papito.

00:05:56.941 --> 00:05:58.609
-Played me.
-[Shark] Not cool, man.

00:05:58.693 --> 00:05:59.694
Betrayed me.

00:05:59.777 --> 00:06:01.863
Hey. Hey, listen. It's just business.

00:06:01.946 --> 00:06:03.239
-You're...
-[Shark] Shady.

00:06:03.322 --> 00:06:04.907
-You're...
-Shady.

00:06:04.991 --> 00:06:06.409
Let it out, buddy.

00:06:06.492 --> 00:06:10.121
-You're the perfect woman!
-["Crimson and Clover" plays]

00:06:10.204 --> 00:06:12.540
She out-snaked the snake.

00:06:12.623 --> 00:06:17.628
If that's not true love, well, then,
I don't know what true love is.

00:06:17.712 --> 00:06:19.172
[music ends]

00:06:19.255 --> 00:06:21.549
Snake... [sighs]

00:06:21.632 --> 00:06:23.843
Okay. Kitty... [stammers]
...you mind telling us

00:06:23.926 --> 00:06:25.219
what we're doing here?

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:28.556
Cutting to the chase. I like it.

00:06:28.639 --> 00:06:30.808
We're planning something big.

00:06:30.892 --> 00:06:32.268
Only problem?

00:06:32.351 --> 00:06:34.562
It's too big for the three of us.

00:06:34.645 --> 00:06:37.148
You need work. We need extra hands.

00:06:37.231 --> 00:06:41.486
Professionals, you know?
With a specific set of skills.

00:06:41.569 --> 00:06:44.530
One last job.

00:06:45.031 --> 00:06:46.657
Whatcha say?

00:06:46.741 --> 00:06:47.742
[chuckles] What do we say?

00:06:47.825 --> 00:06:49.577
No, uh, is the short answer.

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:51.996
But, well, we're flattered.
But the thing is, you know--

00:06:52.079 --> 00:06:53.164
-We're good now.
-[Piranha] Yeah.

00:06:53.247 --> 00:06:54.874
We don't steal stuff anymore.

00:06:54.957 --> 00:06:56.584
Yeah, so if you can just,
you know, untie us,

00:06:56.667 --> 00:06:58.211
and, uh, we'll let ourselves out.

00:06:58.294 --> 00:07:00.505
And we can just call it
a noche, okay?

00:07:00.588 --> 00:07:01.589
[chuckling]

00:07:04.091 --> 00:07:05.927
[laughing]

